{"title":"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(technical_vector_bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (technical vector bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Pair_Sum)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Pair Sum)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Physics-Inspired)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Physics-Inspired)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Complex_Number)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Complex Number)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Extreme_Case)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Extreme Case)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(⚡️3_min_solve⚡️)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (⚡️3 min solve⚡️)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_-_MaffyTaffy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 - MaffyTaffy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb7357b61f4675a08fba468cf3435375a034c5d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = 90^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b207baa53bbc22cebe8d56c0312dd786d93bfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA = BC = \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"21\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fcaa089b53c8f304e51b4fe0291f8c65cc78e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, P_2, \\dots, P_{2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> lie on hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be799cc2c4eb262effbf2a6b196232643b1d4068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP_1= P_1P_2 = P_2P_3 = \\dots = P_{2023}P_{2024} = P_{2024}C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"385\" height=\"17\" />. What is the length of the vector sum \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daafe683a70517576b26bb2a80fdb220002fc49c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overrightarrow{BP_1} + \\overrightarrow{BP_2} + \\overrightarrow{BP_3} + \\dots + \\overrightarrow{BP_{2024}}?\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce37c2b628c51bca492480054b5e30ffbb73162f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }1011 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1012 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }2023 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }2024 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }2025 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"525\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28technical_vector_bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(technical_vector_bash)\">Solution 1 (technical vector bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (technical vector bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us find an expression for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />- and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-components of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/4386be6c68e0550f59fdb174eba65dbc0d39d0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{BP_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf13a0135d960514958da6393175b99c9fc4f7fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP_1+P_1P_2+\\dots+P_{2023}P_{2024}+P_{2024}C=AC=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"400\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ce279b9f30a1f7332c3194926d61906ef03b10c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP_1=P_1P_2=\\dots=P_{2023}P_{2024}=P_{2024}C=\\dfrac2{2025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"387\" height=\"38\" />. All of the vectors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/65951294b3fb380a8ec3ef270bd29f102d5cfa4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{AP_1},\\overrightarrow{P_1P_2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"24\" /> and so on up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97ad04a76b33470586601b9ddd010ebd8af2e496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{P_{2024}C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"24\" /> are equal; moreover, they equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/409717d28124d940122a2edd014c29b04309eb49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf v=\\left\\langle\\dfrac1{\\sqrt2}\\cdot\\dfrac2{2025},-\\dfrac1{\\sqrt2}\\cdot\\dfrac2{2025}\\right\\rangle=\\left\\langle\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}{2025},-\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}{2025}\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"404\" height=\"55\" />. \n</p><p>We now note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61e710a43aa350e6895042cc93217470250041df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{AP_i}=i\\textbf v=\\left\\langle\\dfrac{i\\sqrt2}{2025},-\\dfrac{i\\sqrt2}{2025}\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"229\" height=\"55\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> copies of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae371741ccd912462e74214b31f22e481ee93b08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"9\" /> added together). Furthermore, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba8f1e2a1976db603936ccb4f53565c94ac805a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{BP_i}=\\overrightarrow{BA}+\\overrightarrow{AP_i}=\\left\\langle0,\\sqrt2\\right\\rangle+\\left\\langle\\dfrac{i\\sqrt2}{2025},-\\dfrac{i\\sqrt2}{2025}\\right\\rangle=\\left\\langle\\dfrac{i\\sqrt2}{2025},\\sqrt2-\\dfrac{i\\sqrt2}{2025}\\right\\rangle.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"577\" height=\"55\" /> \n</p><p>We want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/272aabbb86a5ca638e3043d7a4492603dda108e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{2024}\\overrightarrow{BP_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"63\" height=\"55\" />'s length, which can be determined from the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />- and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-components. Note that the two values should actually be the same - in this problem, everything is symmetric with respect to the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0110f1bb04c51b2a4d431bf14489fc1b48b37421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />, so the magnitudes of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />- and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-components should be identical. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-component is easier to calculate. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b7a0cb72970f4bf95c85216bd0c2340b37b4f8d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{2024}\\left(\\overrightarrow{BP_i}\\right)_x=\\sum_{i=1}^{2024}\\dfrac{i\\sqrt2}{2025}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}{2025}\\sum_{i=1}^{2024}i=\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}{2025}\\cdot\\dfrac{2024\\cdot2025}2=1012\\sqrt2.\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>One can similarly evaulate the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-component and obtain an identical answer; thus, our desired length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca30584f42885fb1fd345ad0c88dfc6975c221e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\left(1012\\sqrt2\\right)^2+\\left(1012\\sqrt2\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{4\\cdot1012^2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"434\" height=\"45\" />. \n</p><p>~Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the average vector sum is 1. Multiplying the 2024 by 1, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Pair_Sum.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Pair_Sum)\">Solution 3 (Pair Sum)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Pair Sum)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024_amc12A_p7.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9e/2024_amc12A_p7.png/600px-2024_amc12A_p7.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"338\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9e/2024_amc12A_p7.png/900px-2024_amc12A_p7.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/9e/2024_amc12A_p7.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> reflect over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67859e3c87b664468c453a2c18c714cf6a9307f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{AC} \\longrightarrow B&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We can see that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d312769e92d35fe4d1776f62dc1994d130ff5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left|\\overrightarrow{BP_n}+\\overrightarrow{BP_{2025-n}}\\right|=\\left|\\overrightarrow{BB&#39;}\\right|=2.\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"35\" />\nAs a result, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/372529082b9233fbfbac441c62963358ec9e572b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left|\\overrightarrow{BP_1}+\\overrightarrow{BP_2 }+ ...+\\overrightarrow{BP_{2024}}\\right|=2 \\cdot 1012=\\fbox{(D) 2024}\\]\" width=\"395\" height=\"34\" />\n~lptoggled  image\n</p><p>edited by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the Pythagorean theorem, we can see that the length of the hypotenuse is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There are 2024 equally-spaced points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, so there are 2025 line segments along that hypotenuse. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b05a30e686c21f7fba5ea250f7d7297e7eb252f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{2025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" /> is the length of each line segment. We get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af34d5c128dd70d8bd41de8e691743a1204463b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2}{2025}+\\frac{4}{2025}+...+\\frac{4048}{2025} = \\frac{2}{2025} \\cdot \\frac{2024*2025}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 2024}.\\]\" width=\"483\" height=\"38\" />\nNOTE: This solution seems to have misunderstood the problem and counted line segments from A, arriving at the correct answer by luck.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Physics-Inspired.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Physics-Inspired)\">Solution 5 (Physics-Inspired)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Physics-Inspired)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin, and set the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axes so that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> axis bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axis is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70427c9c73f97d028f34b811c1d91049a017503.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> Notice that the endpoints of each vector all lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ed4b89a6aeb4814026a2be01bde8bd7d264b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />, so each vector is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d9aacf29f31095d387a3c034bf2cc51d0a3282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1i + xj$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" />. Furthermore, observe that for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cdab1f6a1ca191da1bab9271fc8ec476b35dbd4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_k=1i + xj$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f4b7c75a432dfdbf179c8d854ec1264af5c38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_{2024-k} = 1i - xj$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />, by properties of reflections about the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis: therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fd060dd243d4e9bf91525d80266abea07e56d26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_k + v_{2024-k} = 2i.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" /> Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> pairs, the resultant vector is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad4d646aedae10a2b4b309d5f95ebef899434765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012\\cdot 2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />, the magnitude of which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28d84fbbbc02f85c99e90aef4bff9f55dc9d3b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)\\ 2024}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>--Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Complex_Number.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Complex_Number)\">Solution 6 (Complex Number)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Complex Number)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024_amc12A_p7_cn.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/50/2024_amc12A_p7_cn.PNG/600px-2024_amc12A_p7_cn.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"348\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/50/2024_amc12A_p7_cn.PNG 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin, place <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/1/fd1e41063c1a703b5025d5f64c20246b7d83d5a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C= 1+i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce72e89ad391656a12c82e2ca4f87a0c2dc49ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{CP_{1}} = re^{i\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252149e0115a82c456983eaf2d36dd0a39aa73e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{CP_{n}} = nre^{i\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNow we'll find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2feea3bb0d8ca2d4e47b2eb7dd0091361855f72a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$re^{i\\theta}$\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092ca4a3aa2b2295053fe381801e6c6db3d16f66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{|\\overrightarrow{AC}|}{\\text{Number\\;of\\;Equal\\;Segments}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"202\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>= <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5387d313cb2123bc450b7fc4a987c46445365b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{2025} e^{i\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>= <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a4b15f644e68c71ec1277e6a6e503060f5e6085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- \\frac{2}{2025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e2b8ef3030930da4f1cc0cb3b79581f2136ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/3263047c82ecc5bec9a936fa1858df76d6ed0daa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> can be written as such:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6082b2ce9f48d0af93416a87dd775db423ca45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{1} = C + \\overrightarrow{CP_{1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f0b01cff612f6963ff03e37b1bc50400093dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{2} = C + \\overrightarrow{CP_{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>...\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60dfa2387d54a8309b32b24374e45095b79d52e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{2024} = C + \\overrightarrow{CP_{2024}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe want to find the sum of the complex numbers:  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91f1db29a8e35cf347e076a5ca5b0b620c1551c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{1}  + P_{2}  + ... + P_{2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0612ae3e5c02f45f7cc637b67c8d8b9687165baa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 2024c + re^{i\\theta}(1+2+...+2024)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"267\" height=\"22\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d51540543d9f4919a7066a567fcd6dbd181c19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 2024c + \\frac{2024\\cdot2025}{2} \\cdot re^{i\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"220\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNow we can plug in our value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2feea3bb0d8ca2d4e47b2eb7dd0091361855f72a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$re^{i\\theta}$\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c30a81cba59d2e81ba9a9a55d6314b99f816d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024c + \\frac{2024\\cdot2025}{2} \\cdot re^{i\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"201\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b74105d35be255817c1d3937830cbf35bbe1bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 2024 (1+i) - 2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/215404be897697ea29553acaf3625974cce29805.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 2024i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>So the length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/1745df5a9e8241554c15ac584554aae4ecc6948e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(D) 2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"77\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Extreme_Case.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Extreme_Case)\">Solution 7 (Extreme Case)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Extreme Case)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that we can put points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> with odd numbers i on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and those with even numbers i on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. So the sum of vectors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44e6d60c90ab954ecf64c8040003d43a15008470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{BP_1} + \\overrightarrow{BP_2} + \\overrightarrow{BP_3} + \\dots + \\overrightarrow{BP_{2024}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"24\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c611f5727bcbb3b60fc42434b89d82b50f6c88b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012 \\times (\\overrightarrow{BC} + \\overrightarrow{BA})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"25\" /> and the length of vector sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/1745df5a9e8241554c15ac584554aae4ecc6948e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(D) 2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"77\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Emordnilap\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28.E2.9A.A1.EF.B8.8F3_min_solve.E2.9A.A1.EF.B8.8F.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(⚡️3_min_solve⚡️)\">Video Solution 1 (⚡️3 min solve⚡️)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (⚡️3 min solve⚡️)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/abD8gdEI48A\">https://youtu.be/abD8gdEI48A</a>\n</p><p><i>~Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_-_MaffyTaffy\">Video Solution 2 - MaffyTaffy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 - MaffyTaffy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/d8ppdGFdad0\">https://youtu.be/d8ppdGFdad0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A\">2024 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.p